DEBUG ONLY (do not ship): log TEE/enclave results, read the 12th record

Two things, both diagnostic:

1. The driver discards the result of fpc_tee_enroll() and every
   fpc_enclave_process_data() call, so an enrollment whose samples are all
   being rejected still reports "enroll-stage-passed" eleven times and
   "enroll-completed". This logs what they actually return.

2. (Removed again.) Routing the twelfth record through
   sm_wait4img()/fpc_ssm_img_read_cb() instead of patch 0006's own reader was
   tested: fpc_enclave_process_data() returns -1 on that record either way, so
   the rejection is a property of the record and the blob, not of the reader.
   Patch 0006 keeps its own reader, which is bounded by a timeout and so cannot
   hang on a device that sends only eleven.
